0","section":"phrase","kind":"saying","title":"There's no smoke without fire.","html":"<p>If people are saying something, there is usually some truth behind it — used of rumour and suspicion.</p><ul><li>A restaurant keeps getting the same complaint online; the owner insists it is malice, but the inspector books a visit anyway.</li><li>A politician denies a story four times in a week and the press get more interested, not less.</li></ul><p>ES: Cuando el río suena, agua lleva.</p><p>The Catalan and Spanish use water, English uses fire — worth two minutes on why. Pairs with the unit's speculation and unsolved mysteries.</p>","link":"","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"nmv97qyzabla41.0","section":"homework","kind":"text","title":"Waiting room – Vocabulary game","html":"","link":"https://as1-design.github.io/improvedlessons/waiting-room-B21.html","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false}]},{"id":"b21-bl.o4","anchor":"o4","label":"Online 4","kind":"online","n":4,"date":"2026-10-16","plan":false,"unit":"Unit 2","title":"","test":"","cancelled":false,"message":"","header":{"goals":[],"activities":[]},"blocks":[{"id":"omv0v8fyitgm4p.0","section":"tasks","kind":"task","title":"Kahoot Challenge","html":"<p>Double comparatives – click the button to open it in Challenge mode</p><p>(For <strong>later</strong> practice: <a href=\"https://create.kahoot.it/details/b2-1-the-the-comparative-structure-in-english-double-comparatives/c94a98b6-05e2-45c5-b1c0-31f33667e134?drawer=\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">create.kahoot.it/details/b2-1-the-the-compara…</a>)</p>","link":"https://kahoot.it/challenge/01887506?challenge-id=87a24c32-d2b6-432e-bac5-53b9eb2f00ce_1792138529381","linkLabel":"","goal":"","book":"","image":"","continued":false},{"id":"amv9tyq266n7ah.0","section":"tasks","kind":"task","title":"Workbook 2A","html":"<p>1 Vocabulary (a, b, c, d, e, f) (p.36-37)</p>","link":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KhhBmSr3_uh